    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Zurich Zebras highlights a clear tier of high-floor options, with **Junior Caminero** (72.81) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (65.71) leading the charge. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a prime number-two spot in the order against a middling starter in Alcantara, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns a significant boost from a favorable platoon matchup against Martin. Despite **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s lower spot in the lineup, his explosive speed profile provides the elite stolen base potential we covet, even with the risk of an elite holder on the mound. Conversely, **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) and **Luke Raley** (62.16) present strong value today; **Luke Raley** is particularly intriguing as he faces a slower delivery from Buehler, which should significantly inflate his aggressive stolen base opportunities.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Hyeseong Kim** (48.21), who sat just outside our starting threshold. While his platoon splits against Soriano were favorable, the optimizer favored the higher lineup placement and base raw projections of **Dillon Dingler** and **Gary Sanchez** in the catcher slots. Our lineup strategy remains cautious regarding elite arms like deGrom, who drags **Yordan Alvarez** down to a 57.58, though his xwOBA profile keeps him in the mix. We are also monitoring the status of **Casey Schmitt**, whose projection relies on an assumed number-three spot; should the final lineup shift him down, his efficiency score will likely regress. We continue to hold **Zac Veen** in the minors and have sidelined **Christian Yelich** and **Colt Keith** due to current unavailability, ensuring our limited daily game caps are preserved for the most efficient contributors like **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**, despite their difficult matchups against Chandler today.",
